# Tile management

## Purpose

`younite.distance_culling_extension` (v2) manages city tile visibility and payload loading using a hybrid culling strategy. All mutations go through the Payload Orchestrator for frame-budgeted execution.

**Starts disabled by default** — enable via web UI toggle.

## Extension location

`source/extensions/younite.distance_culling_extension/`

- `extension.py` — entry point, `scene.loaded` listener, web toggle
- `tile_manager.py` — discovery, hybrid culling loop, orchestrator calls

## Hybrid culling strategy

The active strategy is chosen automatically based on `/younite/camera/viewType` (written by `player_core`):

### First-person — distance-based (`[D]`)

Uses player XZ position and squared distance to each tile centre. Chosen over frustum culling here to avoid RTX path-tracing reconvergence flicker.

| Zone | Distance | State | Orchestrator ops |
|------|----------|-------|-----------------|
| **Active** | 0–500 m | loaded + visible | `show(HIGH)` |
| **Warmup** | 500–700 m | loaded + invisible | `load_prim(BACKGROUND)` + `hide(MEDIUM)` |
| **Outer** | > 700 m | invisible + unloaded | `hide(LOW)` + `unload_prim(LOW)` |

### Bird's eye — show all (`[B]`)

When switching to bird's-eye, all tiles are immediately restored to Active (loaded + visible) via `_show_all()`. No culling runs while in bird's-eye — the loop returns early each tick.

This avoids the lag spikes caused by USD composition re-evaluation and BVH rebuilds during rapid camera panning. When the user switches back to first-person, distance-based culling resumes and gradually unloads distant tiles through the normal cooldown path.

### Hysteresis

Both modes use 15% hysteresis on zone boundaries to prevent flickering.

## Managed tiles

Discovered at runtime after `scene.loaded`:

- **CU_DT tiles** — children of `/World/CU_DT_8km2_Project_Scene/Geometry/`. Each tile has its own **payload arc** (restructured from stacked references via `convert_refs_to_payloads.py`) — **full load/unload supported**, freeing GPU memory.
- **Legacy tiles** — children of `/World/legacy_buildings/`. No payload arcs — **visibility only**.
- **Edited tiles** — `/World/edited_tile_*`. Each has its own payload arc — **full load/unload supported**.
- **Never managed** — Skandinavium, Skandinavium_lights.

Tiles with payload arcs (~132 of ~137) are fully unloaded from VRAM in the Outer zone. Tiles without payloads (legacy) are only hidden.

## Web UI toggle

- **Web → Kit**: `tileCullingToggle` with `{ enabled: true/false }`
- **Kit → Web**: `tileCullingToggleStatus` with `{ enabled: true/false }`
- `tileCullingToggleStatus` registered in `messaging_core_extension` outbound events

Frontend files: `useControlHandlers.ts`, `useCustomEventHandler.ts`, `UIControls.tsx`, `StreamOnlyWindow.tsx`.

## Lifecycle

1. Extension starts disabled, subscribes to `scene.loaded` and `tileCullingToggle`.
2. On `scene.loaded`: `TileManager.discover()` traverses known parent paths, computes bounding-box centres via `UsdGeom.BBoxCache`, records `HasPayload()`.
3. User enables via web UI → `TileManager.start()` begins 1 Hz async loop.
4. Each tick: read view type; in first-person compute per-tile distance zone and issue orchestrator ops (capped at `MAX_OPS_PER_TICK`); in bird's-eye show all tiles and skip culling.
5. User disables → `TileManager.stop()` → all tiles restored to active via `CRITICAL` priority.

## Tuning constants

At the top of `tile_manager.py`:

| Constant | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `VISIBLE_RADIUS` | 50000 | Active zone boundary (distance mode) |
| `WARMUP_RADIUS` | 100000 | Warmup zone boundary (distance mode) |
| `HYSTERESIS_FACTOR` | 1.15 | In/out threshold gap |
| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | 1.0 | Seconds between ticks |
| `MAX_OPS_PER_TICK` | 5 | Cap on orchestrator requests per tick |
| `FRUSTUM_ACTIVE_MARGIN` | 3.5 | NDC active boundary (frustum mode, 1.0 = screen edge) |
| `FRUSTUM_WARMUP_MARGIN` | 7.0 | NDC warmup boundary (frustum mode) |
| `FRUSTUM_HYSTERESIS` | 1.15 | Frustum mode hysteresis |
| `UNLOAD_COOLDOWN` | 10.0 | Seconds tile must stay in OUTER before payload unload |
| `TILE_PARENTS` | — | Parent prim paths to scan |
| `EDITED_TILE_PREFIX` | — | Prefix for edited tile prims |
| `NEVER_MANAGE` | — | Prim paths always kept active |

## Relationship to other extensions

- **Payload Orchestrator** — all mutations routed through it
- **Light Culling** — independent; manages lights on session layer directly
- **Old distance culling / LOD management** — fully replaced by this extension
